users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected in all rendering methods.\r\n\r\nPS: Something I noticed is that when you toggle HDR 2D in Compatibility (where it has no effect), the clear color will become very slightly darker:\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/11053acd-abdb-4be3-9842-068274b8c002)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/14300bfc-3d52-41b0-b74d-0ca390232df2)\r\n\r\nWith HDR 2D disabled, it's `#4d4d4d` while it's `#4c4c4c` with HDR 2D enabled. With Mobile, the opposite phenomenon happens: it's `#4c4c4c` with HDR 2D disabled and `#4d4d4d` with HDR2D enabled. Forward+ has `#4c4c4c` regardless. The intended color is `#4d4d4d` as the default clear color is `(77, 77, 77)`.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102177#pullrequestreview-2584625398","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102177","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102177#pullrequestreview-2584625398"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102177"}},"submitted_at":"2025-01-30T17:44:54Z","commit_id":"d774f697d36688c6a72c05e3344fd98f2eb1c67f"}]